From 1bf5f2473667e071e2c425d98078b3a2978aba29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:32:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] server: fix 2 test_completion.py tests broken by test-only
 bugs, not the server

test_completion_stream_with_openai_library_stops: inherits offline=True
from the module's ServerPreset.tinyllama2() global (create_server fixture),
but overrides model_hf_repo to a real, uncached HF model. With --offline
the server can't download it, so it starts with an empty model path and
dies (return code 1). Fix: set server.offline = False before starting, same
convention already used by test_basic.py, test_router.py and
test_compat_anthropic.py for the same reason. Also raise the startup
timeout to 600s (same convention as test_lora.py/test_infill.py) since the
~2.3GB Q4_K_M download plus load doesn't reliably fit in the 60s default.
Once it starts, the model's actual reply ("Sure! Here's one for you:")
no longer matches the test's exact-punctuation regex ("Sure, here's one
for"), so loosen it to tolerate that while still checking a joke was told.

Reproduces identically on real upstream/master (same missing offline
reset, same regex mismatch), so this is a pre-existing test bug, not a
regression from this fork's changes.

test_n_probs_post_backend_sampling: compares backend_sampling=true vs
false for the same seed and prompt, but the two /completion calls share
a slot, so the second call hits the prompt cache from the first. Cached
vs cold generation for the same seed is a known, already-tracked llama.cpp
bug (test_cache_vs_nocache_prompt is skipped for exactly this: "fails on
linux, need to be fixed"), and it's what was actually producing the
"assert 4... == 2..." token mismatch, not backend sampling itself: with
cache_prompt disabled, backend_sampling true/false match exactly on both
this fork's Vulkan build and unpatched upstream/master's. Fix: pass
cache_prompt: false, the same workaround already used by
test_consistent_result_same_seed and others in this file for the identical
reason.

(While investigating, found that llama_sampler_top_k_backend_apply uses
ggml_top_k, whose result order is documented as unspecified, while the
downstream dist sampler's cumulative-sum draw is order-sensitive -- a real
latent bug when top_k runs in isolation. Not the cause of either failing
test here (cache_prompt: false alone fixes both), and swapping in the
sorted ggml_argsort_top_k has an unassessed perf cost on the hot sampling
path for large vocabs, so left it alone rather than change unrelated
scope.)

Verified: both target tests plus the full test_completion.py (39 passed,
1 skipped: the pre-existing test_cache_vs_nocache_prompt),
test_chat_completion.py (52 passed), test_slot_save.py (13 passed),
test_speculative.py (8 passed), and test_ctx_shift.py (5 passed) all pass
against this fork's Vulkan build.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
---
 tools/server/tests/unit/test_completion.py | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/server/tests/unit/test_completion.py b/tools/server/tests/unit/test_completion.py
index 01732eb163..9d44dd2144 100644
--- a/tools/server/tests/unit/test_completion.py
+++ b/tools/server/tests/unit/test_completion.py
@@ -133,7 +133,8 @@ def test_completion_stream_with_openai_library_stops():
     global server
     server.model_hf_repo = "bartowski/Phi-3.5-mini-instruct-GGUF:Q4_K_M"
     server.model_hf_file = None
-    server.start()
+    server.offline = False  # this model is not pre-cached by load_all(), so it must be allowed to download
+    server.start(timeout_seconds=600)  # large model needs time to download
     client = OpenAI(api_key="dummy", base_url=f"http://{server.server_host}:{server.server_port}/v1")
     res = client.completions.create(
         model="davinci-002",
@@ -148,7 +149,9 @@ def test_completion_stream_with_openai_library_stops():
         if choice.finish_reason is None:
             assert choice.text is not None
             output_text += choice.text
-    assert match_regex("Sure, here's one for[\\s\\S]*", output_text), f'Unexpected output: {output_text}'
+    # the exact punctuation after "Sure" varies across model/quant revisions ("Sure," vs "Sure!"),
+    # so tolerate that while still checking the model actually told a joke instead of running past the stop words
+    assert match_regex("Sure.*here's one for[\\s\\S]*", output_text), f'Unexpected output: {output_text}'
 
 
 @pytest.mark.parametrize("n_slots", [1, 2])
@@ -547,6 +550,7 @@ def test_n_probs_post_backend_sampling():
             "post_sampling_probs": True,
             "seed": 4242,
             "backend_sampling": backend_sampling,
+            "cache_prompt": False,  # TODO: remove this once test_cache_vs_nocache_prompt is fixed
         })
         assert res.status_code == 200
 
